# The musl image only installs a toolchain — `docker/musl.Dockerfile` copies nothing
# from the context. The repository is still tarred and sent to the daemon before the
# build starts, though, and `target/` is a full PROJ/GDAL/MSVC-scale build tree, so
# leaving it out is the difference between a second and a minute of upload.
.dockerignore
target
node_modules
dist
coverage
assets
.git
*.node
*.tgz
